  "id": "Compound::DB04855 - Gene::785",
  "verbalization": "Dronedarone, a class of antiarrhythmic drugs, is shown to bind to Cacna1s and Cacnb1, which are subunits of the voltage-gated calcium channels. These channels are critical for regulating cellular calcium levels, a key process in cardiac and neuronal function. The evidence suggests that Dronedarone interacts with multiple calcium channel subunits, potentially modulating their activity and influencing the function of the calcium channels. The shared involvement of Cacnb4 in the high voltage-gated calcium channel activity indicates that Dronedarone may have a broader impact on calcium signaling pathways. The integrated evidence supports a mechanism where Dronedarone interacts with calcium channel subunits, possibly altering their function and contributing to the regulation of cellular calcium homeostasis. This mechanism is consistent with the observed involvement of Cacnb4 in the pathway, suggesting a potential role in the drug's therapeutic effects.",
